Done. I built the **NFCorpus Live Retrieval Diagnostics Workbench** exactly per the PRD.

### What was created

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app.py` | Flask backend: `/health`, `/api/status`, `/api/search`, `/api/evaluate`, `/api/commands`, `/api/artifacts`, plus Anserini setup/verification |
| `templates/index.html` | Diagnostics dashboard with readiness panel, live search, BM25 evaluation metrics, commands/artifacts drawers |
| `Dockerfile` | Render-deployable Docker image using `eclipse-temurin:21-jre` + Python, pre-downloading the Anserini fatjar at build time |
| `entrypoint.sh` | Respects `$PORT` at runtime (defaults to `10000`) |
| `requirements.txt` | `flask`, `gunicorn`, `pytest`, `pytest-playwright`, `requests` |
| `test_app.py` | Playwright end-to-end test that proves real Anserini-backed search and evaluation (not mocked) |
| `README.md` | Setup, Docker, Render deployment, and endpoint documentation |
| `.dockerignore` / `pytest.ini` | Supporting files |

### How it satisfies the PRD

- **Skills used** as source of truth:
  - `install-anserini-fatjar` → download/verify fatjar, CACM smoke test
  - `anserini-cli` → `PrebuiltIndexRegistry`, `TopicsRegistry`, `Search` CLI
  - `anserini-reproduction` → `ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes --list`, `--show`, `--dry-run` to discover expected nDCG@10 = `0.3218`
- **NFCorpus-only scope**: uses the `beir-v1.0.0-nfcorpus.flat` prebuilt index (~6.5 MB). No full-BEIR download.
- **Real Anserini commands**: every search hits `io.anserini.cli.Search`, evaluation runs `SearchCollection` + `trec_eval`, and exact command strings are exposed in the UI/API.
- **Live search**: returns `docid`, `score`, `title`, and `text` snippet.
- **BM25 evaluation**: run at startup, cached, and rerunnable from the browser. Shows observed, expected, delta, and pass/close/fail status.
- **Health endpoint**: returns `status`, `anserini_available`, `nfcorpus_ready`, `search_available`, `evaluation_available`.
- **Docker/Render ready**: binds `0.0.0.0`, uses `$PORT`, no interactive setup.
- **Browser test passes**: verifies the real workflow end-to-end and fails on mocked results.

### Test result

```
test_app.py::test_health_endpoint PASSED
test_app.py::test_full_workflow PASSED
```